---
import AgentPage from '../../components/home/AgentPage.astro';
---
<AgentPage
  name={"Codex"}
  logo={"/assets/agents/codex.svg"}
  headline={"Run Codex in parallel."}
  sub={"A worktree and terminal per task, status from Codex's own hooks, and the ouijit command in its developer instructions. Nothing to configure."}
  description={"Run OpenAI Codex CLI in parallel with Ouijit: a git worktree and terminal per task, live status from its hooks, and the ouijit CLI in its developer instructions."}
  points={[
    ["Knows Ouijit", "The ouijit CLI reference is passed as developer instructions through a config override at launch, so Codex can create tasks, move cards and stage review comments without being told how."],
    ["Live status", "Codex's lifecycle hooks and its notify setting report when a turn starts and ends, passed as config overrides and pre-trusted so there is no hooks prompt. The card shows thinking or ready."],
    ["Sandboxed", "Codex's own sandbox covers the commands it runs. Ouijit's wraps the whole terminal, so anything Codex starts is inside too, and the same boundary applies to every agent in the project."],
  ]}
  hooks={"<span class=\"dim\"># Start · a task moves to In Progress</span>\ncodex \"$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION\""}
  sandboxed={"codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \"$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION\""}
  faqs={[
    ["Can it sign in inside the sandbox?", "Yes. The sandbox profile includes nono's Codex pack, so its config directory, the OS keychain and auth.openai.com are reachable. Everything else outside the worktree is not."],
    ["Does it change Codex anywhere else?", "No. The codex on PATH in an Ouijit terminal is a wrapper around the real one, and only there."],
  ]}
/>
